// %run and %load typed in the REPL (plan §7f; D16, D25; IPython's %run,
// Thonny's F5): `madc -i` loads this file into the session, then the
// entries in testrepl_runcmd.input run. `%run -i FILE ARGS` runs FILE's main
// with ARGS (the shell's rules) in THIS session, so `base` below is still
// there; `%run FILE ARGS` runs it in a FRESH session, which the engine asks
// its host for (IPython's payload) and the terminal starts — `base` is gone
// after it, FILE's names stay, and a FILE with no main only defines. A file
// that does not open is refused before any restart, so the session survives
// it, and its error shows once. `%load FILE` defines FILE's names and runs
// nothing, its main included.
int base = 1017;
